<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soppeng Regency</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Soppeng Regency is a regency of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a> province in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, with its seat at Watansoppeng. It covers the lands of the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> kingdom of Soppeng, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>-growing realm that from 1582 was allied with Bone and Wajo in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tellumpoccoe">Tellumpoccoe</a>. The area is known for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> weaving and for the large colonies of bats that roost in the trees of Watansoppeng.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/soppeng-regency.jpg" alt="Soppeng Regency" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ukhy142 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bulu_dua.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
